<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeCreateNothing</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to create a null node</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoNode *SilikoNodeCreateNothing(void);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeCreateNothing</function> function creates
a new <type>SilikoNode</type> object representing that the end of input
for a particular rule has been reached or that zero items in a
zero-or-more rule have been read, and that further parsing should be
done by another rule, such as a parent rule.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoNodeCreateNothing</function> returns a pointer to
a new empty <type>SilikoNode</type> object on success, or
<literal>NULL</literal> if there was a memory error.</para>
</refsection>
